# No rejection language (mousavi-site)

Never write that a paper was declined, rejected, unsuccessful, or not accepted. This applies everywhere: news, publications, CV (HTML and TeX/PDF), research, teaching, and any other public page.

If a submission was declined, describe the manuscript only as **submitted**, **in revision**, or **a working paper** as appropriate. Do not name the venue that declined it, and do not imply a failed outcome (for example “in revision after RecSys”).
